WEBVTT

00:00:00.980 --> 00:00:01.980
We're going to win.

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.980
We're a winning team.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.230
Once we're finished eating, 
let's start practicing again!

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.820
What's their deal?

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.950
Why're you unknowns tryin' so hard?

00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:17.330
It's obnoxious!

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.330
Get back there!

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.470
Renpei, you're playin' well today. 
They're really soarin' off your cleat!

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:29.340
Jinko's shocked by—

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.700
Leave me alone, Sunao.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:30.920
You're annoyin'.

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.850
What?

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:41.930
You bastard!

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.990
That was amazing!

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:58.490
All right! The sumo wrestling's helping!

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.110
Good.

00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:49.830
<b>Episode 18    Study</b>

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:47.020
We got the ball back!

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:50.270
Go, Jinko!

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:52.380
Move the ball to the outside!

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:55.210
What're you playin' at, you clods?!

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:57.400
You ain't goin' nowhere!

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:03.370
He went straight through him!

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.230
They're inside Tenjiku's 22-meter line.

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:18.740
I'm gonna kill you.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:25.930
You bald idiot!

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:28.600
How could you let him go through you, you oaf?

00:03:29.290 --> 00:03:34.330
"B-Bald"? You're the bald idiot,
you bald idiot!

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.440
Now, now. Don't fight.

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.910
You can both be bald idiots.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:40.070
Screw that!

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.700
Dammit!

00:03:48.170 --> 00:03:55.210
They made it past the 22-meter line, 
but Tenjiku's defense got out to them quickly.

00:03:57.050 --> 00:03:59.470
Scoring a try won't be easy.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.180
Get the ball to the outside!

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.510
Let the backs go for it!

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:06.650
Matsu!

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.480
<i>No...</i>

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:15.670
<i>Giving the ball to the backs now
won't grab us the try.</i>

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:26.620
Are they going for it?

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:27.880
Captain!

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:29.870
Go!

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.250
Sorry...

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.870
but you're not gettin' past me.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.380
Tenjiku's #8, Seki.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.260
H-He stopped Sekizan?

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:49.890
Captain!

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.390
Pass!

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:55.640
Natsuki?

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.990
You little...

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.490
Help Ise!

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.500
Go, Jinko!

00:05:36.170 --> 00:05:37.150
Try!

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:43.300
We did it!

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.860
Ise!

00:05:45.900 --> 00:05:48.930
Natsuki! Good job!

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:49.780
Mutsumi-san.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:53.070
Ise! What are you? A forward?

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:01.090
Good job, Ise.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:03.710
Thank you, sir!

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.760
All right! We can do it!

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.380
Kifune, you'll kick for the conversion.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.380
Let's get another one!

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:10.720
Y-Yes, sir.

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:21.650
I can't believe their center
made a play there.

00:06:21.650 --> 00:06:23.490
I underestimated them.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:26.490
Jinko's better than I thought.

00:06:27.410 --> 00:06:29.740
Jinko's #8 is good.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:31.750
We might wanna watch out for him.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:35.130
Why're you touchin' my stomach?

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:37.300
It helps me relax.

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:41.750
Let's take this a little more seriously now.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:48.590
Nice kick, Kifune! We're tied now!

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.600
They really are useless. 
Completely useless.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:56.710
I hope they all die.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.910
There's ten minutes left in the first half!

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.860
Keep it up, Jinko!

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.860
All right!

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:11.710
Matsu-san, use the backs in the next play!

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:12.870
Okay, okay.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.450
Jinko's on a roll.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.900
I don't want Osaka looking down on us.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:21.500
As another team from Kanagawa, 
we need them to win.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.830
Kibucchi!

00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:29.880
<i>Since we're inside the 22-meter line, 
we should start by taking more territory.</i>

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:37.390
Is he trying to put it into touch?

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:42.730
A quick throw-in...

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:46.740
What? But the ball went over the line.

00:07:46.740 --> 00:07:51.820
Sometimes, you can throw the ball in
 even if it goes into touch.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:53.790
{A: Gion o Gion, please learn to enunciate or not say anything}That...

00:07:58.070 --> 00:07:59.500
Renpei, pass!

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:02.410
God, you're annoyin'.

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:08.000
You're all so annoyin'...

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:10.760
Die, idiots!

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.260
What?

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:23.870
Drop goal!

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.460
A drop goal?

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.030
Seriously?

00:08:31.420 --> 00:08:34.030
Wow, he made it.

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.780
That had to be at least fifty meters...

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:39.780
Renpei!

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:44.370
Why'd you go for the drop goal?
 That's only three points!

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.670
They just scored seven with a try!

00:08:47.670 --> 00:08:50.880
It's common sense to pass the ball 
to us and repay them for it—

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:55.630
I went for goal because 
you forwards're useless!

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.640
Quit complainin'.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.890
Keep your mouth shut if you can't score.

00:09:03.620 --> 00:09:06.860
Wh-Who d'you think you are?

00:09:06.860 --> 00:09:08.650
Renpei, that's enough.

00:09:08.650 --> 00:09:09.830
What?

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:12.990
That was a little harsh. 
You shouldn't say things like that.

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.740
And Captain, it's still three points.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:18.980
Let's score where we can.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:23.830
Hey, are they fighting?

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:26.530
Why? They just scored.

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.210
Stop fighting!

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:35.300
Tenjiku's an interesting team.

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.550
I wish we could play them.

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:41.290
They'd be a great match for us.

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:46.090
Tradition, huh?

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.510
Suna-chan...

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:56.270
I hate to ask, but why d'you
 defend Renpei so much?

00:09:58.740 --> 00:10:04.150
We've been friends for 12 years now. 
I can tell what's goin' on in his head.

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:07.620
He's not a bad guy.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:13.030
I hear ya, Suna-chan.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:21.550
Tenjiku's players are all skilled individuals.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:25.400
They're all playing well.

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:29.390
But that makes their deficiencies
 stand out even more.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:34.650
Since they're a new school, 
they lack tradition.

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:38.430
Tradition colors the team's personality.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:42.660
The team's personality dictates 
the team's style of play.

00:10:43.060 --> 00:10:47.660
But Tenjiku, which has yet to
identify its distinct style of play,

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.970
has somehow ended up with
a bunch of talented individuals.

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:56.670
That's why the team clashes internally
instead of coming together.

00:10:59.170 --> 00:11:02.350
Tenjiku is scattered.

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:06.430
Buckteeth!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:07.720
Hosoyan!

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:08.590
Get it out!

00:11:13.430 --> 00:11:15.570
Another pass didn't connect?

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.520
Seki...

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:20.460
Renpei.

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:25.150
Th-The captain told you 
to stop kickin' it just now.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:26.880
I can't catch that.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:31.550
Are you blaming me for 
your own shortcomings?

00:11:32.740 --> 00:11:35.090
N-No, but...

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.590
You buck—

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.190
The first half is over!

00:11:47.820 --> 00:11:49.390
We're three points behind!

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:50.770
All right!

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:52.140
We're just getting started!

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:53.630
Let's go, Renpei.

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:54.690
Die.

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:58.860
Tenjiku

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:00.240
A'right, we're winnin'.

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.240
Jinko

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:03.240
Let's build on our lead in the second half.

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:04.610
Ren—

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:12.820
Suna-chan...

00:12:15.530 --> 00:12:20.510
I can't do it. I don't understand him.

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:28.010
<b>I've told you before: 
My name's Ki-fu-ne!</b>

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:31.020
<b>I have to call you 
that so you match 
with Ebucchi!</b>

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:31.020
<b>SPRINT</b>

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.020
<b>What's 
the point
 of that?</b>

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:35.020
Why did you start fighting during the game?

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:36.740
Who's the culprit?

00:12:41.810 --> 00:12:43.530
Well, whatever.

00:12:43.530 --> 00:12:45.380
I get the picture.

00:12:45.880 --> 00:12:49.660
Don't ever do anything as
counterproductive as fighting again.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:51.000
Hikaru.

00:12:51.810 --> 00:12:54.670
I don't think the first half went poorly.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.360
I believe in you.

00:12:56.900 --> 00:12:58.280
I'm trusting you with the second half.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:12:59.670
Yes, sir.

00:13:01.610 --> 00:13:04.420
Why didn't Futami-san <i>say</i> anythin'?

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:09.070
Don't you think it was harsh of him to put 
everything on the captain's shoulders?

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:10.570
He's supposed to be the coach.

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:14.430
I'll ask again. Why're 
you touchin' my stomach?

00:13:15.130 --> 00:13:17.320
Well, it ain't important.

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:18.690
Ow, ow, ow...

00:13:17.320 --> 00:13:19.450
I like being able to do what I want.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:23.540
I chose a new school so I could do just that.

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:28.100
Sunao!

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:30.060
What is it?

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:33.200
Whose side are you on?

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:34.330
What?

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.440
"Whose"...?

00:13:36.440 --> 00:13:39.310
What are you talkin' about?
We're all on the same side.

00:13:39.310 --> 00:13:41.240
Do somethin' about Renpei!

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:44.810
You're childhood friends, right?

00:13:44.810 --> 00:13:48.090
He's messin' up Tenjiku's stride!

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:52.350
I'm the captain! Make him listen to me!

00:13:57.060 --> 00:14:02.480
I don't think that's somethin' 
a captain should say.

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:05.360
Futami-san said the same thing.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.950
I don't think we're playin' poorly.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.730
Let's do our best in the second half.

00:14:13.690 --> 00:14:17.620
Renpei's brusque and has a bad attitude...

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:22.700
But he wants to win more than any of us.

00:14:23.160 --> 00:14:25.380
That should be enough.

00:14:30.310 --> 00:14:32.250
What's wrong with them?

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:34.330
Idiots.

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:41.440
What do you think of the team
that made the Osaka quarters?

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:48.110
That was a good try.

00:14:51.150 --> 00:14:53.950
Watching you boys lit a fire inside me.

00:14:54.380 --> 00:14:56.710
That's exactly what you should be doing.

00:14:58.170 --> 00:15:01.740
Keep it up during the second half. Got it?

00:15:01.740 --> 00:15:03.080
Yes, sir!

00:15:04.390 --> 00:15:08.000
But this is still a practice game.

00:15:08.000 --> 00:15:13.090
I want as many of our players as possible 
to take on Osaka's quarterfinalists.

00:15:13.750 --> 00:15:16.930
So I'll be making some substitutions.

00:15:18.900 --> 00:15:21.140
The second half will begin shortly.

00:15:22.300 --> 00:15:25.080
All right!

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:28.070
Are you incapable of 
playing without shouting?

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:30.680
Gion?

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:33.030
Yes. Is there a problem?

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:34.950
Oh, no...

00:15:36.770 --> 00:15:38.980
I wonder how this will turn out.

00:15:39.970 --> 00:15:42.830
Not knowing is half the fun.

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:46.130
Good work, Hyosu-san.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:49.590
Hey, Kibi. It sucks that 
you don't get to play.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:54.040
Yeah, but there's a lot I can learn 
by watching from the sidelines.

00:15:54.040 --> 00:15:55.770
That's the spirit. Proud of you.

00:15:59.770 --> 00:16:01.380
Begin the second half!

00:16:06.010 --> 00:16:07.860
<i>I'm pissed.</i>

00:16:08.500 --> 00:16:11.490
<i>The forwards will score this time.</i>

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:38.430
He's fast.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:42.580
Gion's sweeps are fast.

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:49.440
When a guy's tackled to the ground, 
his opponents rush in to take the ball.

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:52.240
Getting them out of the 
way is called sweeping.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:55.710
The faster a sweep, the better.

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:57.620
That way, you can get the ball out sooner.

00:16:58.840 --> 00:17:00.430
If you spend time in a ruck,

00:17:00.430 --> 00:17:03.530
not only is it more likely that 
the ball will be taken from you,

00:17:03.530 --> 00:17:07.250
but more and more players gather 
until their defense is absolute.

00:17:08.430 --> 00:17:11.760
In the area around a ruck,
 you need to play low.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:16.010
It might be the perfect job for Gion.

00:17:33.190 --> 00:17:37.070
Gion, you have one job this time.

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:40.700
Help your teammates when they get tackled.

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.700
Be the first one to the ball.

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:48.460
Be the first one to the ball.

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:53.540
He didn't play in their last game.

00:17:56.100 --> 00:18:02.150
They might actually be able to beat
one of Osaka's quarterfinalists.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:14.630
Gion seems calmer than before.

00:18:15.150 --> 00:18:16.090
Yeah.

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:18.890
Help your teammates.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:20.970
Be the first one to the ball.

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:28.060
But no matter how skilled you are, 
it's impossible to save everyone.

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:32.650
Look closely to see if 
you can save them or not.

00:18:32.650 --> 00:18:37.720
If a teammate's tackled near you, 
push him forward, too.

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:41.860
If you can make it there 
by running, go.

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:43.300
If not, don't.

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:45.970
You absolutely must not waste any energy.

00:18:47.070 --> 00:18:49.590
Watch closely. Rely on your instincts.

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:53.980
Assume that if you can get there just a 
little bit quicker and get the ball out,

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:57.900
your team will gain ten meters.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:19:02.490
After that, keep honing 
your senses during the game.

00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:06.490
Watch the movements and listen to
the voices of the players around you.

00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:10.500
Feel the flow of the game.

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.000
Study.

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:16.310
But I don't have my notebook!

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:18.460
Gion, stand further back!

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:24.220
Get the ball back already, forwards!

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:26.430
Quit wastin' time, you dolts!

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:35.610
The backs moved up?

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:38.300
<i>The team's mood ain't lookin' good.</i>

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.360
<i>We need to build a bigger lead.</i>

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:43.240
<i>I've gotta get the ball back!</i>

00:19:47.190 --> 00:19:49.750
<i>If I pass the ball, 
their defense will crush us.</i>

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:03.160
Did he panic and just kick the ball?

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:06.510
But Tenjiku's wings are 
strong against high punts.

00:20:08.340 --> 00:20:09.330
Ukyo!

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:11.390
Yeah, I got it!

00:20:13.650 --> 00:20:15.520
Ukyo!

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:41.590
Captain!

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:42.760
Taku!

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.360
Try!

00:21:01.020 --> 00:21:02.930
Yeah!

00:21:02.100 --> 00:21:04.360
We turned this around!

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:05.940
All right!

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:10.870
Okay!

00:21:11.390 --> 00:21:13.370
Captain, that was amazing!

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:18.520
Wow, wow, wow!

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:14.970
Taku.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:17.050
Nice kick.

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:19.630
I kicked it because you were there.

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:22.010
Kifune.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:24.990
The position's not great, 
but can you make the conversion?

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:26.880
I-I'll be fine.

00:21:28.900 --> 00:21:31.480
H-Hikaru, I'm sorry...

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:34.060
Don't apologize.

00:21:34.060 --> 00:21:38.580
So we don't have to apologize 
when the other team scores?

00:21:39.800 --> 00:21:41.730
Weak.

00:21:41.730 --> 00:21:42.570
Sorry.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:45.210
Don't apologize! Let's go!

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:50.030
<b>Next Time: "I'm Not Crying"</b>

00:23:46.020 --> 00:23:48.540
Next time: "I'm Not Crying."
